  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 108 AM MST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nNorthwest flow will arrive tonight with initial qpf amounts \nlooking light. The stronger push arrives Friday night into \nSaturday. QPF amounts in the Snake Plain and Magic Valley will \nmost likely range from 0.05 to 0.20 inches but could approach \n0.30 inches if the system is wetter than expected. The eastern \nhighlands and central mountains do much better in this pattern \nwith 0.25 to 0.50 inches most likely but if the system is wetter\nthan expected 0.50 to 1.00 inches is certainly possible and \nupper elevations could easily exceed 1.00 inches. This is a warm\nsystem with accumulating snow above 6500 feet. 1 to 3 inches is\nmost likely but some upper elevations could see 6 to 12 inches.\n\n\nSaturday night and most of Sunday look dry. Another system arrives \nMonday with light precipitation possible. Then the bigger system for \nnext week looks like it will be a split flow type system with heart \nof the system passing to our south. So for now precipitation amounts \nlook very light, but that could easily change as run to run \nconfidence has been virtually nonexistent.",
